What is Ingress?
Ingress is a Kubernetes API object that manages external HTTP and HTTPS access to services within the cluster. Instead of exposing each service separately, Ingress lets you define centralized routing rules.

 • Ingress Resource – Defines routing rules (e.g., host/path-based routing)
 • Ingress Controller – Watches and applies Ingress rules (e.g., NGINX, Traefik)
 • Ingress Deployment and Service – Required to deploy and expose the controller
 • ConfigMap – Used to configure the behavior of the Ingress controller
 • TLS – Supports SSL termination using certificates
 • Authentication – Enables securing routes using auth headers or secrets

Hands-On Practice –
 • Deployed NGINX Ingress Controller
 • Created sample applications and exposed them using Ingress
 • Tested routing using path-based access
 • Understood how Ingress interacts with core networking

Key Takeaway
Ingress helps simplify and centralize external traffic routing in Kubernetes clusters. It becomes essential when managing multiple services and securing traffic at the edge.
